R-H4 R-H9 R-I3 R-I5 R-AD18 R-AD19 R-AD21 R-AD22 R-AD31 R-AD38 R-C1 R-SC6 R-SC16 R-H1 R-H3 R-SE7 R-EC2: slice 015, the unmanaged entries (a path entry, a foreign URL) in `install`, `update` and `add` (`install` with names is `tln add`, R-SP18). 11 runs on 3 projects.
Project `unm` (app): the platform acme/pf 0.1.0, `json` is a path entry (`./json/main.roc`, with a comment on its line), `other` is a foreign URL, `parser` is acme/parser 1.0.0. Its `talon.toml` has keys of the 2 unmanaged aliases (`json = "^2"`, `other = "roc-lang/http@^9"`, and an `[overrides]` key of `other`). Project `key` (app): the platform acme/pf 0.1.0 and `json` as a path entry; its `talon.toml` has `json = "^2"`. Project `plat` (app): the platform is a path entry (`./pf/main.roc`).
Run 1 (R-H9 row 1, R-I5): `install` with no names: the keys of the unmanaged aliases are no want and no constraint, so there is nothing to change. Run 2 (R-H9 row 1): `update` with no names moves the release entries (parser and the platform) and keeps the path entry and the foreign URL byte for byte (the diff of `unm/main.roc` has no line for them).
Run 3 and 4 (R-H9 row 2, slice 009 G3): `update json` (a path entry) and `update other` (a foreign URL) are exit 2. The message says that Talon never changes it and names `tln add <name> --as <alias>`. No index call, no write.
Run 5 and 6 (R-H9 row 3, R-AD21): `install json` and `install other` change nothing: exit 0, the line prints the value as written and names no command. Run 7 (R-H9 row 2, R-AD22): `install json@^2` (that is `tln add json@^2`) is exit 2, as `update`.
Run 8 (R-H9 row 4, R-AD18): `install acme/json`: the default alias `json` is the path entry, so Talon stops (exit 2) and the message says that `--as json` replaces it. The index of acme/json is read first (the alias check follows the pick of the candidates), no write.
Run 9 (R-H9 row 5, R-AD38): `install acme/json@^2 as=json` replaces the whole path entry with acme/json 2.1.0 (2.2.0 is 1 day old, 3.0.0 is outside `^2`). The comment of the line stays. The check and the build run (R-AD38). The note and the line `~ json: ./json/main.roc -> acme/json 2.1.0` name the old value. The key `json = "^2"` of `talon.toml` is the same as the range of the selector (R-AD26), so the file does not change.
Run 10 (the bug of G-never-change, R-AD31): `install acme/pf platform` (that is `tln add --platform acme/pf`) over a path platform: the entry is replaced under its alias, the keyword `platform` and the comment stay, the note is `platform changes: ./pf/main.roc -> acme/pf 0.1.1`. Before slice 015 it was exit 1 (`Internal`: `Set` refuses a path row).
Run 11 (Q1 of the slice review, R-AD38, R-I3, R-C1): `install acme/json as=json` with no selector, in project `key`. The path entry `json` has a key `json = "^2"` in `talon.toml`. The key stays and is the range of the new entry, so the pick honors it: the entry gets acme/json 2.1.0, the newest release inside `^2` (2.2.0 is 1 day old, 3.0.0 is the newest but outside the range). `talon.toml` does not change (no selector writes nothing, R-AD24).
